From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Placeholder Author <placeholder@example.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 1970 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cc_wrapper: handle response files without trailing newline

bash `read` returns non-zero at EOF when the final "line" lacks a
trailing newline, which silently skips the loop body for that line.
Some build systems (e.g. meson 1.10.1, when generating ninja link
response files) emit @rsp files without a trailing newline, so the
sanitized tmpfile ends up empty and clang is invoked with no
arguments.

Use the standard `read ... || [ -n "$opt" ]` idiom so the final,
unterminated line is also processed.

Anchored against toolchains_llvm v1.5.0; also applies cleanly at
v1.7.0 with a 9-line offset under `patch -p1` (the surrounding
context inside the `while` loop is identical at both tags).
---
 toolchain/cc_wrapper.sh.tpl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/toolchain/cc_wrapper.sh.tpl b/toolchain/cc_wrapper.sh.tpl
--- a/toolchain/cc_wrapper.sh.tpl
+++ b/toolchain/cc_wrapper.sh.tpl
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@ for ((i = 0; i <= $#; i++)); do
     # Create a new, sanitized file.
     tmpfile=$(mktemp)
     CLEANUP_FILES+=("${tmpfile}")
-    while IFS= read -r opt; do
+    while IFS= read -r opt || [ -n "${opt}" ]; do
       opt="$(
         set -e
         sanitize_option "${opt}"
